diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..a2a59ac 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,50 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Authentication and passkeys
+
+Use Node.js 24 or newer. Install with `pnpm install`, then run `pnpm dev` for
+local development. The app is served under `/devtools-times/`.
+
+- `/signup`: register with a discoverable passkey or a password.
+- `/signin`: sign in with a passkey button, browser autofill, or a password.
+- `/account`: create, list, rename, and remove passkeys; verify identity;
+  update account details; and sign out. Sensitive changes require verification
+  within the last five minutes. Removing the only sign-in method is blocked.
+
+The original remote password demo did not establish an application session.
+These flows now use the application's SQLite account store for both passwords
+and passkeys. Accounts in the old remote demo service are not automatically
+imported; they require an account migration before use with this backend.
+
+Configuration:
+
+- `AUTH_ORIGIN`: exact origin (scheme, host, optional port), without a path.
+  Set this to the deployed HTTPS origin. The RP ID is its hostname. Defaults
+  to the configured production site; development uses the local request origin.
+  For a local production build, use `AUTH_ORIGIN=http://localhost:11224 pnpm start`.
+- `AUTH_DB_PATH`: SQLite database filename; defaults to `./data/auth.sqlite`.
+  Mount this directory on persistent storage and back it up. This implementation
+  targets a single Node instance. Multiple replicas need a shared transactional
+  database; ephemeral Cloud Run filesystems do not persist accounts across restarts.
+
+WebAuthn requires HTTPS (or localhost). Credential verification uses
+[SimpleWebAuthn server](https://simplewebauthn.dev/docs/packages/server).
+The browser uses native WebAuthn APIs with `webauthn-polyfills` for JSON and
+capability compatibility. Optional Signal APIs are feature-detected and do not
+block account operations. Provider metadata is a small snapshot from
+[passkey-authenticator-aaguids](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids);
+it is used only for display, with a generic fallback for unrecognized providers.
+
+Sessions use opaque random HttpOnly, SameSite cookies, rotate on sign-in, and
+expire after seven days. Challenges expire after five minutes and are consumed
+once, even on failed verification. All mutation endpoints validate the Origin
+header. Passwords are salted and hashed with scrypt. Session/IP request limits
+are applied; configure the reverse proxy to preserve the client address and
+apply additional edge rate limiting for production traffic.
+
+Run `pnpm test` to build and exercise the real HTTP endpoints using signed
+virtual authenticator responses. Tests cover registration, discoverable sign-in,
+reauthentication, ownership, replay/counter checks, expiry, origin checks,
+management, logout, and password fallback without opening a browser.
